FIRST COMMIT PAST THRESHOLD: 89d86da58ad7e69bdc6827c6f8999985e8903185
89d86da58 2026-08-10
fix(core): prevent Prism from swallowing code due to quotes in comments (fixes #1222) (#1234)

* fix(core): func_start Invocation Shield missing for 6 languages -- closes #1221

`func_start`'s method-shorthand/bare-signature branch had no requirement
that a real body/terminator follow, unlike this same file's own `args`
regex (which already implements this "Invocation Shield" for the identical
ambiguity). Any bare call statement at true line start (`next();`) was
therefore misidentified as a function/method definition -- confirmed on
real corpus code (expressjs/express: ~15% of reported JS functions were
phantom call-sites).

Fixed for javascript, typescript, java, apex, dart, and groovy, each with
a fix shape tailored to that language's own legitimate leniency
requirements (zero-prefix constructors, interface/abstract stubs ending in
bare `;`, etc. -- see each rule's own inline comment). csharp is
deliberately left untouched: its func_start already defers this exact
check to a detector.py pipeline-level post-hoc terminator scan (#789),
confirmed independently robust end-to-end.

Also fixes a Rule-14-shaped ReDoS regression the typescript fix's first
draft introduced (two adjacent unbounded whitespace quantifiers separated
by an optional group) -- bounded, confirmed back to linear scaling.

tests/golden_master_audit.json / tests/golden_master_zero_dep_audit.json
regenerated via tests/tools/update_golden_master.py: the ~80-repo corpus
diff (2213 differences, both full-precision and zero-dependency modes)
is entirely composition/tech_debt/impact drops for javascript, typescript,
java, dart, and groovy directory groups -- exactly the expected signature
of removing phantom function counts, no unrelated languages affected.

